{"v": 1, "key": "cu-cu03", "cards": [{"id": "u3.t.plasmid", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">PLAS<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">mid<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"plasmid\" data-audio=\"audio/plasmid.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: plasmid\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"plasmid\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><ellipse cx=\"92\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"70\" ry=\"30\" class=\"f6 d\"/><ellipse cx=\"92\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"65\" ry=\"26\" class=\"f3 k\"/><ellipse cx=\"92\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"60\" ry=\"21\" class=\"f1\"/><path d=\"M80 58 Q90 45 105 55 Q115 68 98 70 Q80 68 80 58\" class=\"f4\"/><circle cx=\"130\" cy=\"62\" r=\"6\" class=\"f5 k\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">plasmid: small extra ring of DNA<\/text><line x1=\"130.0\" y1=\"100.0\" x2=\"130.0\" y2=\"70.0\"/><polygon points=\"130.0,70.0 132.2,74.5 127.8,74.5\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A small ring of extra DNA in a bacterium, often carrying genes such as antibiotic resistance.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>质粒<\/b>：细菌中一小环额外的 DNA，常带有抗生素耐药性等基因。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">plasmid = a little &quot;plasma&quot; ring.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">小环状 DNA。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Can plasmids move between bacteria?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Yes, for example during conjugation.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u3.t.flagellum", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">fla<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">GEL<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">lum<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"flagellum\" data-audio=\"audio/flagellum.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: flagellum\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"flagellum\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><ellipse cx=\"92\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"70\" ry=\"30\" class=\"f6 d\"/><ellipse cx=\"92\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"65\" ry=\"26\" class=\"f3 k\"/><ellipse cx=\"92\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"60\" ry=\"21\" class=\"f1\"/><path d=\"M160 60 Q170 44 180 60 Q188 74 196 58\" class=\"s\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">flagellum: spins to swim<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A long whip-like tail that moves a cell. In bacteria it spins like a propeller. Plural: flagella.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>鞭毛<\/b>：推动细胞运动的长鞭状结构；细菌的鞭毛像螺旋桨一样旋转。复数 flagella。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">flagellum = Latin for whip.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">flagellum 在拉丁语里是「鞭子」。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: What does a flagellum do?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">It moves the cell.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u3.t.pilus", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">PI<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">lus<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"pilus\" data-audio=\"audio/pilus.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: pilus\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"pilus\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><ellipse cx=\"92\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"70\" ry=\"30\" class=\"f6 d\"/><ellipse cx=\"92\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"65\" ry=\"26\" class=\"f3 k\"/><ellipse cx=\"92\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"60\" ry=\"21\" class=\"f1\"/><line x1=\"58\" y1=\"32\" x2=\"54\" y2=\"18\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"80\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"78\" y2=\"16\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"108\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"16\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">pili: stick to surfaces or pass DNA<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A short hair-like projection on a bacterium used to stick to surfaces or to pass DNA. Plural: pili.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>菌毛<\/b>：细菌表面短短的毛状突起，用来黏附表面或传递 DNA。复数 pili。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">pilus = hair.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">pilus 意为「毛」。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Give one job of a pilus.<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Attaching to surfaces, or passing DNA in conjugation.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u3.t.capsule", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">CAP<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">sule<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"capsule\" data-audio=\"audio/capsule.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: capsule\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"capsule\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><ellipse cx=\"92\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"70\" ry=\"30\" class=\"f6 d\"/><ellipse cx=\"92\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"65\" ry=\"26\" class=\"f3 k\"/><ellipse cx=\"92\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"60\" ry=\"21\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">capsule (dashed outer layer)<\/text><line x1=\"40.0\" y1=\"100.0\" x2=\"40.0\" y2=\"78.0\"/><polygon points=\"40.0,78.0 42.2,82.5 37.8,82.5\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A sticky outer layer around some bacterial cells that protects them and helps them stick.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>荚膜<\/b>：部分细菌细胞外一层黏黏的保护层，帮助附着。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">capsule = a protective case.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">capsule = 保护壳。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: What is a capsule for?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Protection and sticking to surfaces.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u3.t.ribosome", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">RI<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">bo<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">some<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"ribosome\" data-audio=\"audio/ribosome.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: ribosome\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"ribosome\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><ellipse cx=\"92\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"70\" ry=\"30\" class=\"f6 d\"/><ellipse cx=\"92\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"65\" ry=\"26\" class=\"f3 k\"/><ellipse cx=\"92\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"60\" ry=\"21\" class=\"f1\"/><circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"55\" r=\"2\" class=\"k\"/><circle cx=\"85\" cy=\"66\" r=\"2\" class=\"k\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"52\" r=\"2\" class=\"k\"/><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"70\" r=\"2\" class=\"k\"/><circle cx=\"130\" cy=\"62\" r=\"2\" class=\"k\"/><circle cx=\"78\" cy=\"48\" r=\"2\" class=\"k\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">ribosomes (dots) build proteins<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A tiny structure that builds proteins. All cells have them.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>核糖体<\/b>：制造蛋白质的微小结构，所有细胞都有。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">ribo = from RNA, soma = body.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">ribo = 核糖，soma = 小体。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Do prokaryotes have ribosomes?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Yes. All cells do.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u3.t.coccus", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">COC<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">cus<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"coccus\" data-audio=\"audio/coccus.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: coccus\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u3-coccus.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"615\" alt=\"Staphylococcus, round bacteria (cocci), under an electron microscope. Each ball is about 1 micrometre wide.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Staphylococcus, round bacteria (cocci), under an electron microscope. Each ball is about 1 micrometre wide.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">电子显微镜下的葡萄球菌（球菌）。每个小球直径约 1 微米。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: Content Providers(s): CDC/ Matthew J. Arduino, DRPH Photo Credit: Janice Haney Carr · Public domain · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Staphylococcus_aureus_VISA_2.jpg\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"coccus\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"60\" r=\"20\" class=\"f3 k\"/><circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"60\" r=\"20\" class=\"f3 k\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"60\" r=\"20\" class=\"f3 k\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">cocci: round<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A round or sphere-shaped bacterium. Plural: cocci.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>球菌<\/b>：圆形或球形的细菌。复数 cocci。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">coccus = Greek kokkos = berry.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">kokkos = 浆果：圆圆的。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Which shape is a coccus?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Round (a sphere).<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u3.t.bacillus", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">ba<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">CIL<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">lus<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"bacillus\" data-audio=\"audio/bacillus.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: bacillus\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u3-bacillus.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"582\" alt=\"Rod-shaped E. coli bacteria (bacilli) under an electron microscope. Each rod is about 2 micrometres long.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Rod-shaped E. coli bacteria (bacilli) under an electron microscope. Each rod is about 2 micrometres long.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">电子显微镜下的棒状大肠杆菌（杆菌）。每根长约 2 微米。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: Photo by Eric Erbe, digital colorization by Christopher Pooley, both of USDA, ARS, EMU. · Public domain · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:E_coli_at_10000x,_original.jpg\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"bacillus\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><ellipse cx=\"60\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"30\" ry=\"12\" class=\"f3 k\"/><ellipse cx=\"140\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"30\" ry=\"12\" class=\"f3 k\"/><ellipse cx=\"100\" cy=\"90\" rx=\"30\" ry=\"12\" class=\"f3 k\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">bacilli: rods<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A rod-shaped bacterium. Plural: bacilli.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>杆菌<\/b>：棒状的细菌。复数 bacilli。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">bacillus = little rod.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">bacillus = 小棍子。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Which shape is a bacillus?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Rod-shaped.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u3.t.spirillum", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">spi<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">RIL<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">lum<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"spirillum\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: spirillum\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u3-spirillum.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"600\" alt=\"Spiral-shaped bacteria under a microscope.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Spiral-shaped bacteria under a microscope.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">显微镜下的螺旋形细菌。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: Wolframm Adlassnig · Public domain · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Spirillen.jpg\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"spirillum\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M20 40 Q40 15 60 40 T100 40 T140 40 T180 40\" class=\"k\"/><path d=\"M20 80 Q40 55 60 80 T100 80 T140 80 T180 80\" class=\"k\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">spirilla: spirals<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">corkscrew-shaped cells<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A spiral or corkscrew-shaped bacterium. Plural: spirilla.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>螺旋菌<\/b>：螺旋形或开瓶器形的细菌。复数 spirilla。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">spiral = spirillum.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">spiral 即螺旋。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: What shape is a spirillum?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">A spiral.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}], "quiz": [{"id": "cu.q.u3.t.plasmid", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A small ring of extra DNA in a bacterium, often carrying genes such as antibiotic resistance.”<\/i>", "opts": ["plasmid", "methanogen", "obligate parasite", "anaerobic"], "a": 0, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>plasmid<\/b>: A small ring of extra DNA in a bacterium, often carrying genes such as antibiotic resistance. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">质粒<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u3.t.flagellum", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A long whip-like tail that moves a cell. In bacteria it spins like a propeller. Plural: flagella.”<\/i>", "opts": ["flagellum", "nitrogen fixation", "mutualism", "pathogen"], "a": 0, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>flagellum<\/b>: A long whip-like tail that moves a cell. In bacteria it spins like a propeller. Plural: flagella. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">鞭毛<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u3.t.pilus", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A short hair-like projection on a bacterium used to stick to surfaces or to pass DNA. Plural: pili.”<\/i>", "opts": ["nitrogen fixation", "binary fission", "pilus", "microbiome"], "a": 2, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>pilus<\/b>: A short hair-like projection on a bacterium used to stick to surfaces or to pass DNA. Plural: pili. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">菌毛<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u3.t.capsule", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A sticky outer layer around some bacterial cells that protects them and helps them stick.”<\/i>", "opts": ["capsule", "microbiome", "spirillum", "aerobic"], "a": 0, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>capsule<\/b>: A sticky outer layer around some bacterial cells that protects them and helps them stick. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">荚膜<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u3.t.ribosome", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A tiny structure that builds proteins. All cells have them.”<\/i>", "opts": ["pilus", "biofilm", "lysogenic cycle", "ribosome"], "a": 3, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>ribosome<\/b>: A tiny structure that builds proteins. All cells have them. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">核糖体<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u3.t.coccus", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A round or sphere-shaped bacterium. Plural: cocci.”<\/i>", "opts": ["nucleoid", "spirillum", "coccus", "retrovirus"], "a": 2, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>coccus<\/b>: A round or sphere-shaped bacterium. Plural: cocci. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">球菌<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u3.t.bacillus", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A rod-shaped bacterium. Plural: bacilli.”<\/i>", "opts": ["bacillus", "thermophile", "microorganism", "microbiome"], "a": 0, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>bacillus<\/b>: A rod-shaped bacterium. Plural: bacilli. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">杆菌<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u3.t.spirillum", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A spiral or corkscrew-shaped bacterium. Plural: spirilla.”<\/i>", "opts": ["spirillum", "biofilm", "mutualism", "ribosome"], "a": 0, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>spirillum<\/b>: A spiral or corkscrew-shaped bacterium. Plural: spirilla. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">螺旋菌<\/span>", "whys": null}]}